From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:43:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PROTOTYPE pco: enable the preamble by default

Local experiment for amazon-suez, never to be sent (Imagination declines
LLM-generated code in src/imagination).

With the vertex-preamble fix (29693961815) the preamble renders correctly
under zink and is the largest single win on GX6250 (a wlroots colour
layer 28.5 -> 8.6 ms). Turn it on unless SUEZ_PCO_NO_PREAMBLE is set, so
the packaged driver needs no PCO_DEBUG in the session environment. The
switch is part of the pipeline cache key.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/imagination/pco/pco_debug.c            | 6 ++++++
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c | 1 +
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/imagination/pco/pco_debug.c b/src/imagination/pco/pco_debug.c
index 0da01774eb1..052aa0e122d 100644
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_debug.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_debug.c
@@ -82,6 +82,12 @@ static void pco_debug_init_once(void)
 {
    /* Get debug flags. */
    pco_debug = debug_get_option_pco_debug();
+
+   /* PROTOTYPE (amazon-suez): the experimental preamble is on by default;
+    * SUEZ_PCO_NO_PREAMBLE=1 turns it off again.
+    */
+   if (!getenv("SUEZ_PCO_NO_PREAMBLE"))
+      pco_debug |= PCO_DEBUG_PREAMBLE;
    pco_debug_print = debug_get_option_pco_debug_print();
    pco_skip_passes = debug_get_option_pco_skip_passes();
 
diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
index 879b225ff0f..3bb6d705797 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
@@ -3041,6 +3041,7 @@ pvr_gfx_pipeline_cache_key(const struct pvr_device *device,
    pvr_gfx_cache_hash_str(&ctx, "SUEZ_PVR_CWE");
    pvr_gfx_cache_hash_str(&ctx, "SUEZ_PCO_ALWAYS_ISP_FB");
    pvr_gfx_cache_hash_str(&ctx, "SUEZ_PCO_NO_FOLD_SAT");
+   pvr_gfx_cache_hash_str(&ctx, "SUEZ_PCO_NO_PREAMBLE");
 
    _mesa_blake3_final(&ctx, key);
 }
